{{!-- "The masthead" — one card per writer, name over a post count and a place.

	{{> "about/team"}}

THE DESIGNED ROLE LINE IS NOT HERE. The design draws "Founding editor" under each name, and Ghost
has no author-role field — a staff user carries a name, a bio, a location, a website and two
social handles and nothing that means "what they do here". On this publication the role happens to
be the first sentence of each bio, and Handlebars cannot take a sentence off a string. The card
therefore carries the two facts Ghost does hold. Already recorded as a Concession in DECISIONS.md
for the Authors Directory; the same one, on a second Surface.

The guard and the ordering are the masthead's, for the reason partials/pages/authors.hbs sets out
at length: every staff account is an "author" to Ghost, `count.posts` is not filterable on authors
in Ghost 6, and ordering by it descending means the first row's count answers whether anybody has
published at all. --}}
{{#get "authors" include="count.posts" order="count.posts desc" limit="100" as |team|}}
	{{#if team.[0].count.posts}}
		<section
			aria-labelledby="team"
			class="container pt-20">
			<h2
				id="team"
				class="font-ui text-muted border-border mb-6 border-b pb-3.5 text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">{{t "The masthead"}}</h2>

			<div class="grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(230px,100%),1fr))] gap-5">
				{{#foreach team}}
					{{#if count.posts}}
						<a
							href="{{url}}"
							class="border-border hover:border-accent bg-surface text-text block rounded-md border p-[22px] no-underline">
							<p class="font-display tracking-heading text-[19px] leading-[1.22] font-medium">{{name}}</p>

							<p class="text-muted mt-2.5 font-mono text-[11px]">
								{{~plural count.posts empty=(t "No posts") singular=(t "% post") plural=(t "% posts")~}}
								{{#if location}}<span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>{{location}}{{/if}}
							</p>
						</a>
					{{/if}}
				{{/foreach}}
			</div>
		</section>
	{{/if}}
{{/get}}
